<title>USA: Favorable harvest weather for Brazil coffee - WSC.</title>
<headline>Favorable harvest weather for Brazil coffee - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, high pressure aloft in Brazil's coffee belt is expected to stay there this week, preventing any cold air from moving into the area, Weather Services Corp said an update on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies were observed over main growing areas of the belt this morning. Temperatures remained near normal levels with lows in the middle 50's F (low teens C).</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected for the next seven days. Temperatures should slowly turn milder. Low temperatures will be in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C). Some cooler conditions may hit higher elevations.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no damaging cold expected,&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
